{
  "challenge": "PY-002",
  "task": "`frequency_map(items)` gets a list of strings and returns a dict that maps each distinct string to how many times it appears. The starter returns an empty dict.\n\n```python\nfrequency_map([\"A3\", \"b7\", \"A3\", \"a3\"])  # {\"A3\": 2, \"b7\": 1, \"a3\": 1}\n```\n\n- Count every string exactly as written: matching is case-sensitive (`A3` and `a3` are different), and spaces, empty strings and odd strings (such as `__proto__`) are counted like any other.\n- An empty list gives `{}`.\n- Don't print anything.\n",
  "language": "python",
  "file": "frequency_map.py",
  "starter": "def frequency_map(items):\n    counts = {}\n    # Count each item.\n    return counts\n",
  "entrypoint": "frequency_map",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "case-1",
      "input": [
        "a",
        "b",
        "a"
      ],
      "expected": {
        "a": 2,
        "b": 1
      },
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "id": "case-2",
      "input": [],
      "expected": {},
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "id": "case-3",
      "input": [
        "A",
        "a",
        "A"
      ],
      "expected": {
        "A": 2,
        "a": 1
      },
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
